 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Why scratch SQLite",
   "items": [
    "Heavy per-folio formula evaluation runs against a temp SQLite file with a shared, mutex-guarded connection-pool registry \u2014 keeping load off the MySQL primary",
    "A background loader thread migrates each finished formula's rows to MySQL while the loop continues; a final catch-all migration sweeps the rest",
    "The job is idempotent (retry: 0) and runs with Chewy.strategy(:bypass) so reruns are safe and don't hammer Elasticsearch"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "Formulas",
   "items": [
    "FundFormulas are per-fund Ruby snippets evaluated per folio; CommitmentCache exposes cached commitment fields as formula variables",
    "A failing step stamps its error onto AllocationRun.status (truncated to 2000 chars) for the UI to show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Triggers & options",
   "items": [
    "Enqueued from FundsController's Run Allocations action with an AllocationRun for tracking",
    "Options steer the run: run_allocations, explain, generate_soa, statement_for, template_id, fund_ratios, sample, rule_for, tag_list",
    "Statement/SOA generation at the end feeds the shared doc-generation pipeline"
   ]
  }
 ]
}